    "body": "Refreshed onto the refreshed #981 and current main (merges only, plain pushes). Head **8d2304f6** (fork synced at upstream/main 683802be).\n\n**Merges**\n- 5c9f923b - merge of a #981 refresh (with main 683802be). One conflict, `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps`, kept both sides:\n  - `startPreamble`: main's #891 G50 tool clamp / `UNCLAMPED` refusal and #1173 `cssOn`, with #977's G96 S in ft/min under G20 (`sCss / 0.3048`) re-applied onto main's G96 block.\n  - #977's `onPartLoading` beside main's #1026 `onSection` (`seatKnown = false`).\n  - Main's new `cycleSeat` / `chainRapid` write lengths through `xWord` / `zWord`, which already take the document unit.\n  - `git show --remerge-diff 5c9f923b --stat`: `assets/posts/fanuc-lathe.cps | 13 ++-----------`\n- 8d2304f6 - merge of #981's maintainer refresh (47ea06be). It conflicted with the parallel refresh above, so #981's own resolution was taken for every file both refreshes touched. The branch now differs from #981's head only by #977's work, plus one #981-side test fix (next section).\n  - `git show --remerge-diff 8d2304f6 --stat`: wire-iso.cps 6, project/apply.rs 4, project/file.rs 2, tests/units_migrate.rs 23, docs/decisions/902 3 (3+/35-, all \"take #981's side\").\n\n**Commits beyond the merges**\n- c8bad1f9 test: two #977 pins follow main's laws.\n  - The golden `nc/inch/fanuc-lathe/axial_drill.nc` was regenerated: it gains `G00 X0 Z1.1811` after G80. That is main's #1011 exit rapid (the mm golden's `G00 X0 Z30`) in inch. No other golden moved.\n  - In `lathe_post_inch::a_peck_counts_the_inch_increment`, the stream now approaches R before the cycle (`first_move: 1`). Main's #1026 refuses a face cycle that is its section's first motion. The asserted words are unchanged.\n- From the parallel #981 refresh (e528c79c, kept): `lathe_post_css::an_inch_tormach_posts_vc_in_ft_per_min_and_d_in_rpm` now sets the document unit to inch, and the file's `post` helper passes `posting::program_options`. Main's pin made the program inch with an inch machine file, so it **fails on #981's head 47ea06be** (G21 ... S170).\n\n**Gate on 8d2304f6** (macOS, debug, sccache), all green:\n- app: lathe_post_inch, lathe_post_css, lathe_post, lathe_post_g76, lathe_post_tormach, program_units, conformance, golden_cl, units_migrate, mcp_units, mcp, mcp_live, wire_post, posting, fidelity_copies.\n- post: script_fanuc_lathe, lathe_post_refusals, script_wire_iso, script_tormach_lathe.\n- clippy `-p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Earlier, on 5c9f923b, the full `cargo test -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-post` run (389 binaries) failed only on the three items fixed above. One flake: `mcp_live::a_trickling_client_is_dropped_on_the_idle_schedule` (ConnectionReset), green on re-run.\n\n**#1126 must merge after #981** (it carries #981's commits). Once #981 merges, this PR's diff is #977's work plus the `lathe_post_css` fix, unless #981 takes that fix first.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
