    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 8d2304f6d42e28e8a64252d2578a74d1b85c7aa7 -->\n**Delta review (M3, safety tier) at 8d2304f6:** this head is the refresh merges of #981's 47ea06be and of main. No blockers. It is ready for the maintainer to merge **after #981**.\n\n**The merges**\n- **`fanuc-lathe.cps`** was the one conflict, and both sides are kept:\n  - main's #891 `cssCap` and its UNCLAMPED refusal;\n  - the G50 clamp;\n  - #1173's `cssOn`;\n  - the G97 clamp lift;\n  - #977's G96 S on top (`fanuc-lathe.cps:432`), in ft/min under G20 and m/min under G21. The rpm clamps are left unscaled.\n- **`onPartLoading`** sits beside main's #1026 `onSection`.\n- **The second merge** only takes #981's side.\n- **A trial merge with current main is clean.**\n\n**Goldens**\n- Against main, no existing golden changes.\n- Against #981, only the 6 new `inch/fanuc-lathe` goldens are added.\n- **`axial_drill.nc`, word by word against its mm twin:**\n  - G21 → G20, D4 → D0.1575, Z20 → Z0.7874, Z10 → Z0.3937, Q12000 → Q4724;\n  - F0.008 → F0.0003, about 5% slower, as the PR body notes;\n  - the exit rapid G00 X0 Z30 → G00 X0 Z1.1811, which is main's #1011 rapid in inch.\n- `lathe_post_inch` pins every inch word against its mm twin.\n\n**Local results** (merged with main), all passing:\n- `lathe_post` 7, `lathe_post_g76` 8, `lathe_post_css` 10, `lathe_post_inch` 6;\n- `lathe_post_tormach` 8, `lathe_post_tormach_thread` 7;\n- `program_units` 7, `golden_cl` 27, `conformance` 6, `recorded_post_streams` 5, `tormach_lathes` 2, all `turning*` suites;\n- `script_fanuc_lathe` 15, `recorded_streams` 12;\n- clippy is clean on app and post.\n\n**Mutations**\n- Dropping the ft/min conversion fails `surface_speed_is_feet_per_minute_and_rpm_never_scales`.\n- Dropping the G50 clamp fails 3 `lathe_post_css` tests and `css_then_live`.\n\n**Notes (not blocking)**\n- Only that one test guards the ft/min conversion.\n- The inch output hasn't been run on a real control. Before real use, run one inch facing program and one inch G76 program in a lathe simulator, or air-cut them.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
